;; M4N slice 2 (docs/m4n-contract.md): a recursive reader over an edited
;; negated input.  Gaining blk(Z) kills base rows and cascades across
;; sweep rounds; the corpse-driven versions probe ~blk at ABSENT-EVER so
;; instantiations against a gained blocker stay owned by the round-1
;; anti-delta version alone (the double-decrement hazard case is the
;; (r 1 3)/(e 3 4)/blk(4) instantiation in the mixed flush).

table (e int int)
table (blk int)
table (r int int)

rule
(e X Y)
~(blk Y)
-->
(r X Y)

rule
(r X Y)
(e Y Z)
~(blk Z)
-->
(r X Z)
